{
  "headline": "Advance voter turnout increases for Toronto's 2026 municipal election",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Advance voting for Toronto's 2026 municipal election saw 222,550 eligible voters participate during a six-day period that ended on October 11, 2026, at 7 p.m. According to CBC Toronto, this represents the largest advance voter turnout in over a decade and a nearly 72 per cent increase compared to the 129,000 early votes recorded during the 2023 mayoral byelection. Election day is scheduled for October 26, 2026. On that day, eligible voters must cast ballots at their assigned voting places as indicated on their Voter Information Card or the Toronto Elections webpage. Voters who requested to vote by mail were required to return completed packages to Toronto Elections by noon on October 14, 2026. To meet this deadline, voters were advised to use one of 25 secure, indoor yellow Toronto Elections Mail-in Voting drop boxes located in each ward across the city. These boxes are monitored by CCTV, inspected regularly, and emptied daily by Elections staff. Voters can verify if a Mail-In Voting package was received on time using a confirmation code. Additionally, registration for third party advertisers, which includes any person, corporation, or trade union intending to spend money to promote, support, or oppose a candidate, closed at 4:30 p.m. on October 9, 2026. Registrations were to be filed in person at the Toronto Elections City Hall office at 100 Queen St. W., first floor, Permit Alley."
    },
    {
      "text": "A recent survey from Liaison Strategies conducted during the advance voting period suggests incumbent Mayor Olivia Chow leads the mayoral race by five points, polling at 51 per cent among decided and leaning voters. Councillor Brad Bradford is polling at 46 per cent. In response to the turnout and polling, Chow’s team credited the results to the efforts of volunteers campaigning across the city to encourage supporters to vote. Conversely, Laryssa Waler, a spokesperson for Bradford’s campaign, stated that the high early turnout indicates voters are not waiting until October 26 to make up their minds."
    }
  ]
}

