  "headline": "Bangladesh parliamentary committee discusses Ganges Water Sharing Treaty",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "A parliamentary standing committee on the Ministry of Water Resources in Bangladesh discussed the nation's interests regarding the Ganges Water Sharing Treaty during its second meeting at the Jatiya Sangsad Bhaban. Chaired by Mohammad Shafiqul Haque Milon, MP, the committee discussed whether the existing treaty would be renewed or continue, though a press release indicated that no final decision has been taken and the relevant process is ongoing. The committee expressed hope that the Padma Barrage project could be inaugurated in February 2027 and discussed a proposed inspection of the project site in Sujanagar upazila of Pabna district on October 25."
    }
  ]
}

